# DSA & Coding

Interview-focused problem curriculum at `/dsa-coding/`. One page per canonical problem (55 total) across 8 pattern modules.

Reference: `content/dsa-coding/01-arrays-hashmap-two-pointers/two-sum.md`

## Audience

Engineers preparing for coding interviews (3–10 YOE). Assumes [Java Engineering](/java-engineering/) for collections complexity.

## Structure

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `data/dsa_coding_modules.yaml` | 11 modules, 55 problems + guides (auto-generated) |
| `data/dsa_coding_order.yaml` | Flat prev/next (auto-generated) |
| `scripts/dsa_coding_questions_data.py` | Problem registry (single source of truth) |
| `scripts/build_dsa_coding_handbook.py` | Sync yaml + prune orphans |
| `content/dsa-coding/<module>/<slug>.md` | One page per problem (edit markdown directly) |

## Hugo Front Matter (problem pages)

```yaml
interviewHandbook: true
languages: ["java", "golang"]
source: "https://leetcode.com/problems/..."
sourceLabel: "LeetCode N"
pattern: "HashMap"
module: 1
moduleTitle: "Arrays, HashMap & Two Pointers"
sectionRef: "1.1"
draft: false
```

## Required Sections (`##` headings)

1. **Problem Statement** — restated + constraints table
2. **Pattern Recognition** — signals that identify the technique
3. **Brute Force** — naive approach
4. **Optimal Solution** — final approach summary
5. **Walkthrough** — small example trace
6. **Implementation** — Java + Go in impl-tabs (mandatory)
7. **Complexity** — time and space
8. **Edge Cases** — at least 3
9. **Interview Follow-ups** — 3–5 probes with short answers
10. **See Also** — prev/next + cheat sheet link

Pattern module `_index.md` pages: Mermaid decision flowchart, template pseudocode, problem table.

Module 11 cheat sheets: Recognition Signals · Template · Complexity · Common Mistakes · Top Problems.

